    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's hard to put into words. it's not even like i'm crying all the time. it's just... the math of it doesn't work anymore. my whole routine, my hobbies, the way i talk, even the way i think about the future... it was all built around him. now that he's gone, there's no foundation. i feel like i'm just floating in this empty space, waiting for something to happen, but i know nothing is gonna happen. it feels pointless to even try to build a new version of myself. what's the point of starting over when the original version is just dead?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The math doesn't work because the equation was always a shared one, and now one side is gone. What you're feeling isn't just grief; it's the sudden, brutal realization that your entire structure was dependent on another person. Trying to build something new when the foundation is gone is exhausting, and you don't have to pretend it's easy. Sometimes, the only true point is in the quiet, in letting the weight of that emptiness just settle, without the pressure to fill it.",
      "source": "target",
